## Schema (LLM)

### GraphQL Schema

- [GraphQL Schema Reference (v2.1)](https://developer.jtl-software.com/cloud/api-reference/erp/v2.1/graphql-schema.md): Complete GraphQL SDL schema for the JTL ERP API v2.1. Indexed for AI tools (MCP, llms.txt) to enable accurate query and mutation assistance.
- [GraphQL Schema Reference (v2.0)](https://developer.jtl-software.com/cloud/api-reference/erp/v2.0/graphql-schema.md): Complete GraphQL SDL schema for the JTL ERP API v2.0. Indexed for AI tools (MCP, llms.txt) to enable accurate query and mutation assistance.

## Vouchers

### Guides

#### Vouchers

- [Vouchers API Quickstart](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/guides/quickstart.md): Set up a client, get credentials, and run through the full voucher lifecycle.
- [Vouchers API Error Codes](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/guides/error-codes.md): Error response format and validation error codes for the Vouchers API.
- [Vouchers API Changelog](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/guides/changelog.md): Version history and breaking changes for the Vouchers API.

### API Reference

#### Overview

- [Vouchers API](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference.md): Create, manage, and redeem vouchers in JTL Voucher Cloud.

#### Endpoints

##### Vouchers

- [Get a list of vouchers](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/get-a-list-of-vouchers.md): This call will give you a paginated list of vouchers.
- [Create a new voucher](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/create-a-new-voucher.md): Use this call to create a new voucher
- [Recharge a voucher](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/recharge-a-voucher.md): Use this call to recharge a voucher. This can be used for example for customer cards. Please note that this call is not used for cancelations of previously charges.
- [Get a voucher](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/get-a-voucher.md): Use this call to get a specific single voucher. Please note that you wont get the vouchers secret properties *code* and *pin* (use the vouchers/{id}/complete call instead).
- [Delete a voucher](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/delete-a-voucher.md): A voucher can only be deleted when it has no charges yet.
- [Update a voucher](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/update-a-voucher.md): Due to security restrictions only the sku and batch property can be updated on inactive vouchers
- [Get a complete voucher](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/get-a-complete-voucher.md): Use this call to get a voucher with its secret properties *code* and *pin*.
- [Set the status for a voucher](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/set-the-status-for-a-voucher.md): This call is used to activate or deactivate a specific voucher.
- [Get a list of voucher charges](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/get-a-list-of-voucher-charges.md): This call will give you a paginated list of voucher charges.
- [Get a charge of a voucher](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/vouchers/get-a-charge-of-a-voucher.md): Use this call to get a specific charge of a voucher.

##### Reservations

- [Set the reservation for a specific voucher](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/reservations/set-the-reservation-for-a-specific-voucher.md): This call temporary reserves an amount on a specific voucher, that can later be charged. A reservation expires after 30 minutes or in case a new one is requested for this voucher.
- [Charge a specific voucher reservation](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/reservations/charge-a-specific-voucher-reservation.md): Charges the previously created temporary reservation on a voucher.

##### Charges

- [Refund a specific voucher charge](https://developer.jtl-software.com/vouchers/api-reference/charges/refund-a-specific-voucher-charge.md): This call is used to (partial) refund a specific charge that was previously done on a voucher (for example if a customer returns goods to the store).

##### Clients
